I chose moderate, oppositely‑signed weights on the position (x) and velocity (x_dot) to pull the cart toward the centre, strong negative gain on sin(θ1) to counter the first pole’s tilt, a positive gain on sin(θ2) (the angle between the links) to drive the second pole back into alignment, and modest negative gains on both angular velocities (θ1_dot and θ2_dot) for damping. The cosine and constraint‑force terms are set to zero to avoid unnecessary bias, and the bias is zero to keep the controller unbiased. These values are deliberately kept low (≈0.3‑2.0) to stay within the action limits, produce smooth, low‑gain PD‑like control, and give the controller a chance to stabilise both poles for many steps.
